I'm relatively new here (rarely pass the Oracle), but for what it's
worth:
I really like this, but the problem is that zapping a wand of nothing
or a discharged other wand (which presumably look indistinguishable to
an observer) is not dangerous to onlookers, so if intelligent monsters
were to behave rationally, there's nothing to be scared of - all you've
done is demonstrate your impotence.

Only when you zap a dangerous wand with remaining charges should an
intelligent monster be scared. (regardless of whether you zap it at
them or not.)

Maybe it would be good to sidestep my objection for the sake of
fun-factor by simply saying that some intelligent monsters won't behave
entirely rationally, and would be scared by seeing you wave a wand
around, regardless of whether you demonstrate it to be a harmless wand
in the process.



